# The emission golden is a recording of bytes, compared byte for byte. `core.autocrlf` is on for
# most people working on this, and it would rewrite the line endings on checkout -- so the file
# only ever matched in the working tree that generated it, and any fresh checkout on Windows went
# red on line 1 with two lines that look identical.
#
# `-text` keeps git out of it. The spec also strips carriage returns when it reads, because this
# only fixes what is checked out from here on, and a copy already converted stays converted
# (`tests/emit_spec.lua`).
tests/emit-golden.txt -text

# The snippet golden is the same kind of file and was already surviving the same way: its checker
# normalizes on read, and its comment records the same failure (`tools/check-snippet-golden.js`,
# passing on the file it had just written and going red after one `git reset`). It is marked here
# so the two goldens are governed the same way, and so a checkout stops being the thing that
# rewrites a recording of bytes.
tools/snippet-golden.txt -text
